            <ArticleTitle>Coronary artery disease in women: the myth still exists, unfortunately.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>215-21</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1097/DCC.0b013e3181ec3731</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>There is a large media effort available in an effort to increase awareness of coronary artery disease in women. Despite this, there is still a misconception among some people and, unfortunately, some health care providers that heart disease is a man's disease. This article reviews some of the information about women as related to coronary artery disease; a short review of the literature, symptoms, diagnostic tests, and treatment pertinent to women; and action nurses can take to help educate the public, and other health care providers, about this deadly threat.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
